   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "-i adjectives also have a past",
     "texto": [
      "In Japanese the -i adjective is conjugated, including in the past. The final **い** changes to **かった**: **おいしい** → **おいしかった です** (was tasty), **たかい** → **たかかった です** (was expensive).",
      "The negative past: **い** → **く なかった**: **たかく なかった です** (was not expensive).",
      "The usual exception: **いい** → **よかった** (was good) and **よく なかった** (was not good)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "The past of -i adjectives",
     "columnas": [
